{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"lint-runner","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Lint Runner","description":"Runs ESLint, Ruff or Stylelint on the open file and paints the problems as underlines with the message on hover.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.1"},"categories":["Linters"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onStartup"],"permissions":["terminal","workspace.read","workspace.write"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"lintRunner.run","title":"Check This File","category":"Lint Runner"},{"command":"lintRunner.list","title":"List Problems...","category":"Lint Runner"},{"command":"lintRunner.next","title":"Go to the Next Problem","category":"Lint Runner"},{"command":"lintRunner.clear","title":"Clear Problems","category":"Lint Runner"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"lintRunner.next","key":"Alt+F8"}],"configuration":{"title":"Lint Runner","properties":{"lintRunner.linter":{"type":"string","enum":["auto","eslint","ruff","stylelint"],"default":"auto","description":"Which linter to use. Auto picks by file type: ESLint for JavaScript and TypeScript, Ruff for Python, Stylelint for CSS."},"lintRunner.onSave":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Check the file every time you save."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Lint Runner: runs ESLint, Ruff or Stylelint on the open file and paints the problems in the editor as colored underlines\n// with the message on hover, a count in the status bar and a list you can jump through. Needs the linter installed in your project.\n// The linter writes its JSON report to .ferrum/lint, which this extension reads.\n\nconst DIR = '.ferrum/lint';\n\nconst LINTERS = {\n  eslint: { name: 'ESLint', exts: 'js jsx mjs cjs ts tsx vue svelte', report: DIR + '/eslint.json', command: (f, r) => `npx eslint -f json -o \"${r}\" \"${f}\"` },\n  ruff: { name: 'Ruff', exts: 'py pyi', report: DIR + '/ruff.json', command: (f, r) => `ruff check --output-format=json --output-file \"${r}\" \"${f}\"` },\n  stylelint: { name: 'Stylelint', exts: 'css scss less', report: DIR + '/stylelint.json', command: (f, r) => `npx stylelint -f json -o \"${r}\" \"${f}\"` },\n};\n\nfunction linterFor(path, forced) {\n  if (forced && forced !== 'auto' && LINTERS[forced]) return forced;\n  const ext = String(path || '').split('.').pop().toLowerCase();\n  return Object.keys(LINTERS).find((k) => LINTERS[k].exts.split(' ').includes(ext)) || null;\n}\n\n/** Turns a linter report into problems: { line, col, endLine, endCol, severity: 'error'|'warning', message, rule }. Lines and columns start at 0. */\nfunction parse(linter, text) {\n  let data;\n  try { data = JSON.parse(text); } catch { return null; }\n  if (!Array.isArray(data)) return null;\n  const out = [];\n  if (linter === 'eslint') {\n    for (const f of data) for (const m of f.messages || []) out.push({ line: (m.line || 1) - 1, col: (m.column || 1) - 1, endLine: (m.endLine || m.line || 1) - 1, endCol: (m.endColumn || m.column || 1) - 1, severity: m.severity === 2 ? 'error' : 'warning', message: m.message, rule: m.ruleId || '' });\n  } else if (linter === 'ruff') {\n    for (const m of data) out.push({ line: (m.location?.row || 1) - 1, col: (m.location?.column || 1) - 1, endLine: (m.end_location?.row || m.location?.row || 1) - 1, endCol: (m.end_location?.column || m.location?.column || 1) - 1, severity: /^(E9|F)/.test(m.code || '') ? 'error' : 'warning', message: m.message, rule: m.code || '' });\n  } else if (linter === 'stylelint') {\n    for (const f of data) for (const m of f.warnings || []) out.push({ line: (m.line || 1) - 1, col: (m.column || 1) - 1, endLine: (m.endLine || m.line || 1) - 1, endCol: (m.endColumn || m.column || 1) - 1, severity: m.severity === 'error' ? 'error' : 'warning', message: String(m.text || '').replace(/\\s*\\([^)]*\\)$/, ''), rule: m.rule || '' });\n  }\n  return out.sort((a, b) => a.line - b.line || a.col - b.col);\n}\n\nconst unsafePath = (p) => /[\"\\n\\r$`]/.test(p);\nconst relative = (root, p) => (root && p.startsWith(root) ? p.slice(root.length).replace(/^[\\\\/]+/, '') : p);\n\nexports._test = { linterFor, parse, LINTERS, relative };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  let problems = [];\n  let types = null;\n  const reg = (id, fn) => context.subscriptions.push(ferrum.commands.register(id, fn));\n  const sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\n\n  types = {\n    error: ferrum.editor.createDecorationType({ textDecoration: 'underline wavy', backgroundColor: 'rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.14)', gutterText: '●', gutterColor: '#ef4444' }),\n    warning: ferrum.editor.createDecorationType({ textDecoration: 'underline wavy', backgroundColor: 'rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.14)', gutterText: '●', gutterColor: '#f59e0b' }),\n  };\n  context.subscriptions.push(types.error, types.warning);\n\n  async function paint(path) {\n    const mk = (sev) => problems.filter((p) => p.severity === sev).map((p) => ({\n      start: { line: p.line, col: p.col },\n      end: { line: p.endLine, col: Math.max(p.endCol, p.endLine === p.line ? p.col + 1 : 0) },\n      hoverMessage: p.message + (p.rule ? '  (' + p.rule + ')' : ''),\n    }));\n    await ferrum.editor.setDecorations(types.error, mk('error'), path);\n    await ferrum.editor.setDecorations(types.warning, mk('warning'), path);\n    const e = problems.filter((p) => p.severity === 'error').length;\n    const w = problems.length - e;\n    ferrum.window.setStatusBar('lintRunner.status', { text: problems.length ? 'Lint: ' + e + ' error' + (e === 1 ? '' : 's') + ', ' + w + ' warning' + (w === 1 ? '' : 's') : 'Lint: clean', tooltip: 'Click to list the problems', command: 'lintRunner.list' });\n  }\n\n  async function lint(quiet) {\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    if (!doc || !doc.path) return quiet ? undefined : ferrum.window.showMessage('Open and save a file first.', 'warn');\n    if (!ferrum.workspace.root) return quiet ? undefined : ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a folder first.', 'warn');\n    const key = linterFor(doc.path, ferrum.settings.get('lintRunner.linter'));\n    if (!key) return quiet ? undefined : ferrum.window.showMessage('No linter is set up for this kind of file. Supported: ESLint (JavaScript, TypeScript, Vue, Svelte), Ruff (Python), Stylelint (CSS, SCSS).', 'warn');\n    if (unsafePath(doc.path)) return ferrum.window.showMessage('The path of this file has characters I will not put in a command.', 'warn');\n    if (doc.dirty) await ferrum.commands.execute('file.save');\n    const l = LINTERS[key];\n    const rel = relative(ferrum.workspace.root, doc.path);\n    await ferrum.workspace.writeFile(l.report, '');\n    await ferrum.terminal.run(l.command(rel, l.report));\n    const t0 = Date.now();\n    let parsed = null;\n    while (Date.now() - t0 < 45000) {\n      await sleep(600);\n      let text = '';\n      try { text = await ferrum.workspace.readFile(l.report); } catch { text = ''; }\n      if (text.trim()) { parsed = parse(key, text); if (parsed) break; }\n    }\n    if (!parsed) return ferrum.window.showMessage(l.name + ' did not produce a report. Is it installed in this project? See the terminal.', 'warn');\n    problems = parsed;\n    await paint(doc.path);\n    if (!quiet) ferrum.window.showMessage(problems.length ? l.name + ': ' + problems.length + ' problem' + (problems.length === 1 ? '' : 's') + '.' : l.name + ': no problems.');\n  }\n\n  reg('lintRunner.run', () => lint(false));\n  reg('lintRunner.list', async () => {\n    if (!problems.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('No problems. Run \"Lint: Check This File\" first.');\n    const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(problems.map((p) => ({ label: p.message, detail: 'Line ' + (p.line + 1) + ', column ' + (p.col + 1) + (p.rule ? '  ·  ' + p.rule : ''), description: p.severity, p })), { placeholder: problems.length + ' problems. Pick one to go there.' });\n    if (pick) await ferrum.editor.setSelection({ line: pick.p.line, col: pick.p.col }, { line: pick.p.endLine, col: pick.p.endCol });\n  });\n  reg('lintRunner.next', async () => {\n    if (!problems.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('No problems recorded. Run \"Lint: Check This File\" first.');\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n    const at = doc ? doc.selection.start : { line: -1, col: -1 };\n    const next = problems.find((p) => p.line > at.line || (p.line === at.line && p.col > at.col)) || problems[0];\n    await ferrum.editor.setSelection({ line: next.line, col: next.col }, { line: next.endLine, col: next.endCol });\n  });\n  reg('lintRunner.clear', async () => {\n    problems = [];\n    await paint();\n    ferrum.window.setStatusBar('lintRunner.status', { text: '' });\n  });\n\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.events.on('save', () => { if (ferrum.settings.get('lintRunner.onSave') === true) lint(true).catch(() => {}); }),\n    ferrum.events.on('activeChanged', () => { problems = []; paint().catch(() => {}); }),\n  );\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Lint Runner\n\nRun your project's own linter on the open file and see the problems **in the editor**: red wavy underlines for errors, amber for warnings, a dot in the gutter, the message on hover, a count in the status bar, a list to jump through (**Alt+F8** goes to the next one).\n\n| Linter | For | Needs |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ESLint | JavaScript, TypeScript, Vue, Svelte | ESLint in your project (`npx eslint`) |\n| Ruff | Python | `ruff` on your PATH |\n| Stylelint | CSS, SCSS, Less | Stylelint in your project |\n\n## How it works, honestly\n\nThe extension cannot read the terminal. It types the linter command in the terminal (you see it) with an option that makes the linter write its **JSON report to `.ferrum/lint/`**, then reads that file and paints the result. If the linter is missing or crashes, no report arrives and you are told to look at the terminal. Turn on `lintRunner.onSave` to check on every save.\n\nUses the **decorations** API (Ferrum 0.3.1 and later).\n\n## Permissions\n\n**terminal** to run the linter, **workspace.read** and **workspace.write** for the report file.\n"}}}